#!/usr/bin/env node
'use strict';
// Emergency Response spot mutations: changes to the rules (which positives get zones, names, the coarse-location
// rule, the edge, the counts, the "nearest" line, the boxes, dates; from E1b the groups, quarantine, the window, the
// weeks and months, the flock sizes and numbers, miles, days since and the GeoJSON; zones.csv and the map picture's
// model, site/emergency/branded.js; the chart's counts and drawing, site/emergency/chart.js; from 2.6 the drawn
// zones: the area, the crossing check, the set shapes, the names, the zone set and the exports' area and source; from
// 2.7 the animal filter and the map picture's counts by layer, the notes, the safety net and the key's room), the
// types, recognition and the page must each fail a suite.
//
// Each mutant changes one exact piece of code in a temporary copy of the repository; the suite named for its group
// must then report failed checks. A suite that stops early does not count as catching it.
//   unit   site/emergency/rules.js, types.js, datasets.js, branded.js, chart.js, map.js's viewBounds (2.4), report.js, message-icons.js and report-form.js (2.9) and site/shared/recognize.js, against the Emergency unit
//          suite (which also compares the rules with the R reference); from 2.4 also tools/work-pc/check_hpai_table.R
//   page   site/emergency/app.js, map.js and index.html (from 2.6 also draw.js and the picture's key row in branded.js),
//          against the Emergency Chrome suite's parts named with the mutant ("page" and "results" unless it names
//          others; from E1b also "e1b", "png", "chart" and "speed"; from 2.3 "overview"; from 2.6 "draw"; from 2.7 "filter";
//          from 2.8 "layers", "cvifilter", "byanimal" and "kinds"; from 2.9 "report", with site/emergency/report-view.js, "form", with report-form.js, and "page2", page 2
//          and the map's badge for a premises detected twice, and "figures", with report-figures.js);
//          from 2.8 the unit group also mutates
//          the how-to (site/emergency/changing-kinds.html, its .txt twin) and types/hpai.js's lines it names
//          (foreground only; about 40 seconds a mutant, so run a few numbers at a time to stay under 600 seconds)
//
// Usage (repository root): node tests/mutation/run_em_mutations.js unit|page [numbers ...]
//                          node tests/mutation/run_em_mutations.js list
//                          node tests/mutation/run_em_mutations.js check [unit|page]
// "check" runs no suite: it looks for every mutant's text in today's files (about a second) and lists each one found
// other than exactly once (stale). In a run, a stale mutant is recorded as stale and the run goes on with the next.
// The unmutated suite runs first in the same copy and must pass. The copy is deleted at the end, and the
// repository's files are checked unchanged (SHA-256). Logs and a ledger: local-test-artifacts/em/mutations/.
// Copied from tests/mutation/run_s11_mutations.js (its copy, run and ledger), with the Emergency suites.
